  "threatModel": "\n## Trust Boundaries\n\n| Boundary | Description |\n|----------|-------------|\n| browser → backend `POST /api/change-password` | An authenticated but restricted session submits new password material here. |\n| route gate → browser (`portal_profile` cookie) | A script-readable, non-credential cookie carrying display information. |\n| Cloudflare edge → origin | After this cutover the edge performs no authentication at all; the tunnel is transport only. |\n\n## STRIDE Threat Register\n\n| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |\n|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|\n| T-01-34 | Elevation of Privilege | the whole portal, once the edge shield is removed | critical | mitigate | The cutover checklist requires a working portal account and a verified post-cutover backend build before the policy is removed, and verifies session-gated status and download access afterwards; the route inventory from plan 01-02 is reviewed as part of the same step |\n| T-01-35 | Information Disclosure | the `portal_profile` cookie | low | accept | It carries only a handle and a display name — values the signed-in member already sees in their own header — and never a token. The session cookie remains HttpOnly and is untouched. |\n| T-01-36 | Spoofing | a forged `portal_profile` cookie | low | accept | It is display-only and grants nothing; every authorization decision reads the HttpOnly session cookie server-side. A forged value changes what the forger sees in their own header and nothing else. |\n| T-01-37 | Elevation of Privilege | the forced-change screen bypassed by editing the URL | high | mitigate | The route gate redirects and the backend extractor independently refuses every non-exempt route for a flagged session — this screen adds no third enforcement point and relies on neither being optional |\n| T-01-38 | Denial of Service | the certificate lapsing after the cutover | high | mitigate | Step 7 of the cutover explicitly verifies the ACME challenge path is reachable with no Access policy gating it, which is what turns STATE.md's dated blocker into a closed item |\n| T-01-39 | Repudiation | a log-out that appears to succeed but leaves a server-side session alive | low | accept | Documented and deliberate: the client fails toward signed-out, and the residual session expires on its own. Server-side teardown of a live session is Phase 3's ADMIN-03. |\n| T-01-SC | Tampering | package installs | low | mitigate | This plan adds no new dependency in either the frontend or the backend |\n",
