  "raw": "---\nphase: 04-bulk-archive-downloads\nplan: 02\ntype: execute\nwave: 2\ndepends_on: [04-01]\nfiles_modified: [backend/migrations/0005_archive_jobs.sql, backend/src/config.rs, backend/src/jobs/mod.rs, backend/src/api/jobs.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/mod.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/local.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/cloud.rs, backend/tests/archive_preflight.rs]\nautonomous: false\nrequirements: [DL-03, HARDEN-01]\nmust_haves:\n  truths:\n    - \"[Flagged assumption DL-03/unclassified] The exact cap boundary, timeout result, duplicate/normalized-name behavior, and capacity snapshot semantics remain assumptions until the preflight tests make each explicit.\"\n    - \"[Flagged assumption HARDEN-01/concurrency] Concurrent malformed and valid job creates cannot bypass the same closed request-validation seam.\"\n    - \"Over-cap, insufficient-space, timeout, invalid, or duplicate-normalized selections insert zero job and manifest rows.\"\n  artifacts: [backend/migrations/0005_archive_jobs.sql, backend/src/config.rs, backend/tests/archive_preflight.rs]\n  key_links: [\"POST /api/archive-jobs -> bounded recursive walk -> capacity check -> one transaction\"]\n  prohibitions:\n    - statement: \"The archive request must not let a member choose the Stage destination or expose `_archives` as member-owned storage.\"\n      status: unverified\n      flagged: true\n---\n<objective>Persist the irreversible ordered-manifest contract and enforce authoritative preflight. Purpose: make every accepted archive deterministic, bounded, and auditable. Output: migration, closed request types, walkers, transaction, tests.</objective>\n<execution_context>@/home/cinedise/.codex/gsd-core/workflows/execute-plan.md</execution_context>\n<context>@.planning/phases/04-bulk-archive-downloads/04-CONTEXT.md\n@.planning/phases/04-bulk-archive-downloads/04-PATTERNS.md\n@backend/src/api/jobs.rs</context>\n<assumption_delta_decision>noun: archive preflight capacity; decision: no-change; the word “also” adds a second check in one request, not a new identity model.</assumption_delta_decision>\n## Artifacts this phase produces\n- `0005_archive_jobs.sql`: Archive action/tool, owner, collection metadata, ordered entries, and omission tables.\n- `CreateArchiveRequest`, `ArchivePreflightError`, `ArchiveManifestEntry`, and closed `OnCollision` wire types.\n<tasks>\n<task type=\"checkpoint:decision\" gate=\"blocking\">\n  <name>Task 1: Confirm the one-way ordered-manifest contract</name>\n  <files>backend/migrations/0005_archive_jobs.sql</files>\n  <read_first>.planning/phases/04-bulk-archive-downloads/04-CONTEXT.md, backend/migrations/0002_jobs_and_audit.sql, backend/src/jobs/mod.rs</read_first>\n  <action>Before implementing D-09, present the exact one-way choice already selected in context: persist normalized `(relative_path,size)` rows ordered deterministically, execute only that snapshot, and compute omissions against it. Confirm proceed; changing to execution-time re-walk would break DL-08 and byte-stable resume.</action>\n  <decision>Authorize the one-way D-09 ordered-manifest persistence contract before its migration is created.</decision>\n  <options>Proceed — persist the ordered manifest as locked in context; Stop — return to phase discussion because changing it invalidates DL-08 and deterministic resume.</options>\n  <resume-signal>Reply `proceed` to authorize the migration, or `stop` to halt execution.</resume-signal>\n  <verify><automated>test -f backend/migrations/0002_jobs_and_audit.sql</automated></verify>\n  <acceptance_criteria>The checkpoint records proceed before any D-09 schema is written.</acceptance_criteria>\n  <done>The executor records `proceed` for the D-09 ordered-manifest contract before creating the migration.</done>\n</task>\n<task type=\"auto\" tdd=\"true\">\n  <name>Task 2: Accept one bounded, authorized archive manifest transactionally</name>\n  <files>backend/migrations/0005_archive_jobs.sql, backend/src/config.rs, backend/src/jobs/mod.rs, backend/src/api/jobs.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/mod.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/local.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/cloud.rs, backend/tests/archive_preflight.rs</files>\n  <read_first>backend/migrations/0002_jobs_and_audit.sql, backend/src/config.rs, backend/src/jobs/mod.rs, backend/src/api/jobs.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/local.rs, backend/src/tiers/browse/cloud.rs, backend/tests/job_scope_enforcement.rs, .planning/phases/04-bulk-archive-downloads/04-RESEARCH.md</read_first>\n  <behavior>- Exact 400 GiB with adequate Stage capacity is accepted; one byte over is refused with real totals.\n- `MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES` defaults to exactly 400 GiB and a valid environment override becomes the authoritative cap.\n- Timeout/cap/capacity/invalid paths/duplicates/unknown cloud sizes insert zero rows.\n- HARDEN-01 rejects malformed/null collision values through a closed enum while valid transfer creates remain compatible.</behavior>\n  <action>Implement D-08/D-09/D-11/D-13/D-14 as a distinct authenticated archive-create request containing only source tier and explicit root paths. Add `Config::max_archive_bytes`, loaded from `MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES` with the locked 400 GiB default, following the existing download-cap convention and covering both default and override in the config tests. Walk local roots through one TierRoot and cloud roots via one bounded recursive rclone listing, never partial totals; normalize and stable-sort names; filter symlinks and `_archives`; validate the configured archive limit and Stage health; then insert job, owner, and manifest in one transaction. Extend existing action/tool enums and SQL closed sets. Fix HARDEN-01 at the shared request boundary without weakening existing transfer contracts.</action>\n  <verify><automated>cd backend &amp;&amp; cargo test archive_preflight -- --nocapture</automated></verify>\n  <acceptance_criteria>All refusal paths are zero-write, accepted manifests are ordered and owner-bound, archive destination is server-computed, source Read is the only member permission required, and regression tests prove the exact 400 GiB default plus environment override.</acceptance_criteria>\n  <done>The archive preflight suite passes, proving deterministic accepted manifests, zero-write refusal paths, owner binding, server-computed destination, and both cap configurations.</done>\n</task>\n</tasks>\n<threat_model>\n## Trust Boundaries\n| Boundary | Description |\n|---|---|\n| member→archive POST | Paths, tier, counts, and JSON are untrusted. |\n| manifest→filesystem | Persisted names describe work but convey no authority. |\n## STRIDE Threat Register\n| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T-04-04 | Elevation of Privilege | archive creation | high | mitigate | Require source Read and server-compute Stage destination. |\n| T-04-05 | Tampering | manifest names | high | mitigate | TierRoot containment plus independent ZIP-name normalization and uniqueness. |\n| T-04-06 | Denial of Service | recursive preflight | high | mitigate | Bound payloads/rows/path lengths and enforce named deadline/cap before transaction. |\n</threat_model>\n<verification>`cargo test archive_preflight -- --nocapture` proves boundaries and zero-write failures.</verification>\n<success_criteria>A valid selection becomes one durable ordered archive job; every invalid/refused selection creates nothing.</success_criteria>\n<output>Create `.planning/phases/04-bulk-archive-downloads/04-02-SUMMARY.md` when done.</output>\n",
